      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 1251: 🔴 The new recovery still relies on `trackedMembers_`/`devices` being current, but the device-listener callback has no tracking-generation check. `stopTracking()` removes the listener only after clearing state, so a callback already copied by `PresenceManager` can run after a later `startTracking()` and `onDeviceOffline()` can erase a freshly re-announced device from the new record. With an empty `devices` set, `std::includes` is immediately true and the peer can be treated as exhausted again, defeating this recovery path. Capture a generation/token when starting tracking and ignore online/offline callbacks from older generations.",
      "revId": "e4ec20161142db7328a9647d8fc6a6345150c8e1",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
